<title>UK: BA Cargo 90pct back to normal after strike.</title>
<headline>BA Cargo 90pct back to normal after strike.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways World Cargo operations are 90 percent back to normal after disruption caused by last week's 72-hour cabin crew strike, said its regional manager Europe Dennis Connolly.</p>
<p>Cargo operations should be fully back to normal by Monday July 21, Connolly said, adding that BA is once again accepting livestock and human remains freight bookings which were suspended for the duration of the strike. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
